From 9e3ea395c9732ee5dc996c3efbbf32e071ec0c27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: titanism <101466223+titanism@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:06:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(deps): stop undici crashing when a peer closes a paused
 response

undici 7.30.x asserts !paused in Parser.finish(), which runs from the socket
"end" (and "close") handler when a response has no Content-Length and is not
chunked, so its body ends when the peer closes. If that body had filled the
response stream past its 64 KiB high water mark before the caller read it, the
parser was paused when the peer closed: the assertion threw as an
uncaughtException ("assert(!this.paused)" on Bree) and the request then hung
until its body timeout. 7.12.0 did not have finish(); it arrived with the
7.30.1 bump.

Backport the undici 8.6.0 finish() into the existing undici patch: resume the
parser and drain what is still buffered on the socket before llhttp_finish(),
instead of asserting. undici stays at 7.30.1 (8.x needs Node 22).

Test serves close-delimited bodies just over the high water mark (plus small
and large controls), reads each after the peer has closed, and checks every
byte arrives. It fails with the same uncaughtException without the fix.
